## 1. Unchanged three-branch proof

Let one exact projective `pi/3` orbit have total mass `W`, with ordered phase masses

\[
C\ge U\ge V\ge0,
\qquad W=C+U+V.
\]

Put

\[
K={2\over\sqrt3},
\qquad r_{crit}=\sqrt{20/29}.
\]

The proof uses exactly the same exhaustive split as the corrected `g=0.0077` theorem.

### Strong branch

While the center/leaf excess ratio is below `r_crit`, use the physical
iterative-pruning pair theorem

\[
\rho\ge {1\over10}(a+b-K)_+^2.
\]

For a fixed total orbit mass `W`, the resulting one-orbit capacity is denoted
`Psi_s(W)`.

### Fallback branch

Past the strong threshold but while `C<=K`, use only the unconditional physical pair
bound

\[
\rho\ge {2\over29}(a+b-K)_+^2.
\]

### High-center branch

For `C>K`, use no physical pair theorem.  The generic triangle-free capacity

\[
E\le C(W-C)
\]

is maximized at the boundary `C=K` throughout the relevant orbit interval.

This is the same scope repair that was independently hostile-audited before the
`0.0077` strengthening.

---

## 2. Exact certificate at `0.007707`

The committed verifier uses only `Fraction` arithmetic, Machin bounds for `pi`, and
integer-square-root enclosures.  It checks the full chain with

\[
C_{707}=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}+{7707\over10^6}.
\]

The strong-branch tangent is taken at the rational point

\[
c_0={935389\over10^6}.
\]

The exact outward checks include:

- the full orbit interval remains below `2K`;
- the strong-branch center/leaf excess ratio remains below `sqrt(20/29)`;
- the left-center derivative remains positive;
- the total strong-capacity derivative in dominant mass remains positive;
- the fallback-boundary derivative remains positive after including the moving
  boundary term;
- the high-center branch remains more than `0.032` below `Delta_2` at the endpoint.

Most importantly, the strong endpoint still has the exact positive margin

\[
\boxed{
\Delta_2-\Psi_s(C_{707})>2\times10^{-7}.
}
\tag{G707.3}

The fallback endpoint remains more than `1.3e-3` below `Delta_2`, so the strong branch
continues to control the scalar ceiling.

The same certificate gives a lower bound above `0.5966` for the load-bearing strong
`W`-slope after residual-square subtraction.  Thus the residual-stability machinery
used downstream at `g=0.0077` remains available with room.

