## 3. Why the value stops at `0.007707`

A non-load-bearing numerical solve puts the strong-capacity zero near

\[
0.00770727\ldots .
\]

The exact margin at `0.007707` is already only about `2.5e-7`; the architecture is
essentially exhausted.  No claim is made at `0.0077072` or at the numerical root,
even though exploratory arithmetic remains positive slightly farther.

The useful consequence is not the seventh decimal itself.  It is that the complete
scope-safe atomic input can now be substituted into the residual survivor system:

```text
C_707 = 2 sqrt(Delta_2) + 0.007707,
(T-q/2)/D >= C_707 - o(1),
T_R/D       >= C_707 - o(1),
sigma_R/D   >= 0.015414 - o(1).
```

The next step is to propagate `C_707` through the already-audited correlated residual
triangle.  Because the previous proof-only floor is `1.843578`, a successful
propagation needs to certify a new rounded endpoint rather than merely restate the
atomic gain.

**Disposition:** proved proof-only matched atomic strengthening. C-II and Level I remain open.
